expected_issues.description:
Potential null/undefined handling: this branch assumes both `asset.fileModifiedAt` and `asset.fileCreatedAt` are non-null `Date`s. If either can be null/undefined (or not a Date), the comparison and subsequent `toISOString()` later can throw. Consider guarding (e.g., prefer available one, else last-resort `asset.createdAt`/`new Date(0)`), and ensure `localDateTime` is always a valid `Date` before logging.

```suggestion
      const created = asset.fileCreatedAt;
      const modified = asset.fileModifiedAt;
      const earliestDate = created && modified ? (modified < created ? modified : created) : (modified ?? created ?? asset.createdAt);
      if (!earliestDate) {
        this.logger.warn(`Asset ${asset.id} has no file timestamps; falling back to current time`);
        dateTimeOriginal = new Date();
        localDateTime = dateTimeOriginal;
      } else {
        dateTimeOriginal = earliestDate;
        localDateTime = earliestDate;
      }
```

